# Copy the pieces you need into the two places that read them, and never commit
# the filled-in files:
#
#   backend/   — the model key. Prefer `dotnet user-secrets`, which keeps it out
#                of the repo entirely (see "Required" below).
#   frontend/.env.local — everything marked "Frontend". Next.js does not read
#                this file, so it has to live there.


# ── Required: a model provider key ──────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The Quickstart reads this with builder.Configuration["OPENAI_API_KEY"], so
# either of these works:
#
#   cd backend && dotnet user-secrets set OPENAI_API_KEY "sk-..."   (preferred)
#   export OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
#
# The agents hard-code their model ids because the doc pages do: gpt-6-luna
# (reasoning effort "none") on the Quickstart, Tool Rendering, State Rendering,
# Shared State and (patched, see README §9.8) Components-as-Tools agents.
# Change them in backend/Program.cs and backend/SharedStateAgent.cs.
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...


# ── Frontend, optional ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These belong in frontend/.env.local.

# Where the runtime reaches the AG-UI server. Use 127.0.0.1 if localhost
# resolves to IPv6 while the agent binds IPv4.
# MS_AGENT_URL=http://localhost:8000

# Read by the three runtime routes copied verbatim from doc Code tabs
# (json-render, hashbrown, open-generative-ui). Set it alongside MS_AGENT_URL
# if you move the backend port.
# AGENT_URL=http://localhost:8000

# Only for /generative-ui/mcp-apps. That page's runtime runs a Node BuiltInAgent
# (openai/gpt-5.4) inside Next.js rather than the .NET agent, so it needs the
# model key here too.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# Turns on the Rich Threads section. Server-side only, and read only by
# frontend/src/app/api/copilotkit-threads. Leave it unset and that endpoint
# falls back to the in-memory runner: the read-only thread routes still answer,
# mutations return 422, and the prebuilt drawer stays locked.
#
# The Quickstart now gets it with `npx copilotkit@latest project select`
# (and writes it to `.env`); this repo reads it from frontend/.env.local.
# CPK_INTELLIGENCE_API_KEY=cpk-...

# Managed Intelligence endpoints. REST and realtime are different hosts, so
# override both or neither. Defaults are correct for the cloud-hosted platform.
# INTELLIGENCE_API_URL=https://api.intelligence.copilotkit.ai
# INTELLIGENCE_GATEWAY_WS_URL=wss://realtime.intelligence.copilotkit.ai

# The bearer token the provider forwards on every AG-UI request, per the
# Authentication page's `headers` prop. Nothing on the .NET server validates it
# — that page's only published .NET validation is JWT bearer against a live
# identity provider. Set this to watch the header go out; see /auth.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_AUTH_BEARER_TOKEN=super-secret-demo-token

# CopilotKit Intelligence public license key (browser-safe). Not needed by any
# route in this repo.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_COPILOTKIT_LICENSE_KEY=ck_pub_...
